   new=r"""A fourth strand, less visible in the healthcare literature but foundational to any verifiable invalidation mechanism, is the cryptographic accumulator and commitment scheme literature. One-way accumulators compress a finite set into a single short value supporting membership testing (Benaloh & de Mare, 1994); dynamic accumulators add efficient revocation and the mathematical machinery for verifiable membership and non-membership proofs over sets that change over time (Camenisch & Lysyanskaya, 2002), surveyed across applications from anonymous credentials and certificate revocation to blockchain-based audit systems (Ren, 2022).""",
